  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"The conductor welcomes observations but decides the musical interpretation; comments can be collected during short pauses without interrupting every attempt.\", \"decision\": \"How should singers offer observations about musical balance?\", \"goal\": \"Make rehearsals easy to attend and prepare for while helping singers use shared rehearsal time effectively.\", \"problem\": \"A community choir is preparing a small program through a series of rehearsals. It has a conductor, willing section leaders, a booking organizer, numbered scores that members may use, and shared practice recordings. The rehearsal room has movable chairs and enough space for short sectional work. Members have varied experience and availability. Musical direction remains with the conductor, and each routine below can operate within any agreed rehearsal schedule.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nSection leaders collect balance observations from their singers and summarize them to the conductor during a short pause. Related concerns reach the conductor together, reducing repetition while preserving information from different parts of the choir.\nThe conductor asks one section at a time what it heard after a combined passage and then decides adjustments. Rotating invitations give each part a clear opportunity to describe the balance from its listening position.\nSingers note balance observations and raise them during a designated discussion pause before the conductor chooses adjustments. Comments accumulate without breaking each attempt, and the conductor can consider several perspectives at one useful stopping point."
    }
  ],
